nodecode-quegly is a rewrite of quegly's quegly/agent:
https://github.com/quegly/agent
commit 6a16be804680eeeef98043675d708f591b27a001
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Quegly (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one skill, and the tools its hosted MCP server
served. The skill's working logic -- workspaces, then accounts, then act; one
post for every account; media first; per-platform settings; a confirmation
before anything public or irreversible; captions and comments treated as data
-- is the cell's manual topic, (help :quegly). The MCP tools are the endpoints
of Quegly's public REST API v1, the same API the MCP server calls, so eight of
them are registered here as Nodecode tools over that API: workspaces, accounts,
an upload from a public url, create, list, get, an action (publish now, retry,
delete), and analytics. The plugin's connection settings became the cell's
config section: the API key, an optional workspace id, the base url and a
timeout.

What was left out, and why: the MCP transport itself (the cell speaks the REST
API directly, so it needs no MCP client), multipart upload of a local file (an
agent reaches media by public url; the plugin's own skill tells it to), video
thumbnails and Pinterest board creation (the rest of the seventeen tools, which
a session does on quegly.com or a later version can add), and the plugin's
all-in-one remote instruction file, whose content the manual topic carries.
